Z||000000||new fiero||08-05-2001||04:05 PM||||As some of you know I have put the L4 Iron Duke from my wrecked 88 coupe into my 86 coupe.  She ran great for the first two weeks but now is back firing when I shift into second and give it gas turning a corner.  Any suggestions/comments?<P>Andy<P>------------------<BR>newfiero<BR>(swapping 88 L4 to 86 and having fun!)<BR>Yahoo! Messenger id: newfiero||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||08-05-2001||04:38 PM||||Check all the vac lines and make sure one hasn't pulled/blown off. If it has cruise, remove it from the vacuum pumbing. There could be a leaking solenoid or diaphragm in it.<P>Cap both lines from the fuel vapor can. if the valve in the can is hungup then you'll have a vac leak.<P>Check/replace the MAP sensor and it's vac line. This vac line must be connected to the correct TBI port with as short a vac line as posible. <P>Check/replace the MAT sensor to the right of the TBI in the intake manifold. Carbon on this sensor can skew the signal to the ECM.<P>MAP and MAT sensors are used to calculate timing and fuel mix.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero_24||08-05-2001||05:33 PM||||I had backfiring, and I replaced the ignition module and it went away.  Autozone should be able to test it for free for you.<P>Craig<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||10
